      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I think it should be remapped to right trigger press in, followed by a directional input. Then the left control stick can be used for moving around.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-02-23T05:58:49.816Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Peace sign, for example, currently triggers just by resting your fingers on A/B or X/Y. However, it also triggers by resting your finger on the control stick. This means that it's nearly impossible to move around without accidentally triggering the gesture.\n\nInstead, I would like the stick to be ignored, with the ability to still use A/B/X/Y for deliberately performing the gesture.\n\nI'm sure some people probably enjoy being able to move around while doing the gesture though, so maybe it would end up having to be optional.",
